Haha, forcing Fira Code on the entire web is definitely a power move! 😄

**Font debate:** IBM Plex vs Fira Code is kinda apples to oranges - IBM Plex is more of a general-purpose font family (sans, serif, mono) while Fira Code is specifically a programming font with ligatures. For coding, Fira Code's ligatures are pretty sweet, but IBM Plex Mono is cleaner if you don't want the fancy symbols.

**"Fira" meaning:** It comes from Mozilla's font family - "Fira" doesn't mean anything specific, it's just their branding. The "Code" variant adds programming ligatures to the base Fira font.

**Firefox OS:** Yeah! Mozilla had Firefox OS (2011-2016) trying to compete with Android/iOS. It was web-based but didn't have Node.js - it used SpiderMonkey (Firefox's JS engine) with some additional APIs for hardware access. It flopped pretty hard because web apps weren't quite ready to replace native mobile apps back then.

